# OMEMO Content Factory — example environment file.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" for local development:
#     cp .env.example .env        (bash)
#     Copy-Item .env.example .env (PowerShell)
#
# NEVER commit your real ".env" — it is git-ignored on purpose (PROJECT.md §6).
#
# Infrastructure configuration only. Secrets stay outside the repository; the values below are
# safe examples/placeholders for the settings implemented through ROADMAP Stage 7.
#
# Variables are read directly from the process environment. A ".env" auto-loader is not part of
# the runtime; export values in the shell or provide them through the deployment environment.

# Application environment: development | testing | production
OMEMO_APP_ENV=development

# Logging verbosity: CRITICAL | ERROR | WARNING | INFO | DEBUG | NOTSET
OMEMO_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Run store (ROADMAP Stage 7, ADR-0026): the SQLite file every Run is saved to.
# Unset or blank -> .omemo/runs.sqlite3 under the working directory (git-ignored).
# OMEMO_RUN_STORE_PATH=.omemo/runs.sqlite3

# Per-role LLM binding, exact token pricing and request budget (ADR-0016/0029/0052). Replace the
# price placeholders with the provider's current Decimal rates per one million tokens; real-provider
# bindings fail closed when any of the five values below is absent or invalid. Fake bindings need
# only OMEMO_PROVIDER__<ROLE>=fake.
# OMEMO_PROVIDER__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=anthropic
# OMEMO_MODEL__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=claude-model-id
# OMEMO_INPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=replace_with_decimal
# OMEMO_OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=replace_with_decimal
# OMEMO_PRICE_CURRENCY__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=USD
#
# The output budget of one answer. There is no default: 2048 used to be hardcoded and is too small
# for a model that thinks — a role that spends the budget on reasoning never emits its structured
# answer, and the Run fails as INVALID. Keep it inside what a non-streaming request can return
# (16000 is a sound starting point; the adapter does not stream).
# OMEMO_MAX_TOKENS__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=16000
#
# Extended thinking, sent explicitly on every request. One of:
#   adaptive        — the current models' on-mode (Opus 5, Sonnet 5, Opus 4.6/4.7/4.8). Recommended
#                     there: thinking is their default anyway, and on Opus 5 explicitly disabling it
#                     can make the model describe a tool call in text instead of calling the tool,
#                     which is how this factory receives every structured answer.
#   disabled        — no reasoning; the whole budget goes to the answer.
#   budget:<tokens> — the pre-adaptive form (>= 1024 and below OMEMO_MAX_TOKENS__<ROLE>), the only
#                     one Haiku 4.5 and older models accept. Rejected with 400 by Opus 5 / Sonnet 5.
#   inherit         — send no thinking field and let the model's own default stand. A deliberate
#                     choice, not a fallback: that default differs between models.
# A model that does not accept the chosen mode answers 400, which surfaces as a managed failed Task.
# OMEMO_THINKING__CONTENT_RESEARCHER_V1=adaptive

# Notion brief board (ROADMAP Stage 9, ADR-0040/0047). All seven are required once the board is used;
# a missing or blank one fails closed. There are no default property names — they are your
# database's own. The token is the integration secret: keep it in ".env", never in the repository.
# OMEMO_NOTION_TOKEN=replace_with_integration_secret
# OMEMO_NOTION_DATABASE_ID=replace_with_database_id
# OMEMO_NOTION_READY_PROPERTY=Stage
# OMEMO_NOTION_READY_VALUE=Ready for production
# OMEMO_NOTION_RUN_STATUS_PROPERTY=Run status
# OMEMO_NOTION_RUN_ID_PROPERTY=Run id
# A property of Notion type "URL" that receives the review Doc's link.
# OMEMO_NOTION_REVIEW_LINK_PROPERTY=Review

# Google Docs review desk (ROADMAP Stage 10, ADR-0043). Both are required once the desk is used;
# a missing or blank one fails closed. The key file is a service account's JSON key — keep it
# outside the repository. Share the folder (preferably on a shared drive) with the service
# account's e-mail as an editor.
# OMEMO_GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=/path/outside/the/repo/service-account.json
# OMEMO_GOOGLE_REVIEW_FOLDER_ID=replace_with_drive_folder_id

# Production service for n8n (ROADMAP Stage 11, ADR-0049). The token is required (32+ characters)
# and must match the n8n "Concept factory service" Header Auth credential (Bearer <token>).
# OMEMO_SERVICE_TOKEN=replace_with_a_long_random_secret
# OMEMO_SERVICE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# OMEMO_SERVICE_PORT=8765

# Generation department — the ending frame (ADR-0066/0067). All three are required once used;
# no default model and no default size. The key is a Gemini API key from Google AI Studio.
# OMEMO_GEMINI_API_KEY=replace_with_gemini_api_key
# OMEMO_GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-image
# One of 512, 1K, 2K, 4K (upper-case K).
# OMEMO_GEMINI_IMAGE_SIZE=2K

# Generation department — the video (ADR-0066/0067). All four are required once used. The key
# pair comes from the Higgsfield console. The model must take an ending frame:
# kling-video/v3.0/std/image-to-video, kling-video/v3.0/pro/image-to-video or
# kling-video/v3.0/4k/image-to-video (Turbo does not). Sound is "on" or "off".
# OMEMO_HIGGSFIELD_API_KEY_ID=replace_with_key_id
# OMEMO_HIGGSFIELD_API_KEY_SECRET=replace_with_key_secret
# OMEMO_HIGGSFIELD_VIDEO_MODEL=kling-video/v3.0/pro/image-to-video
# OMEMO_HIGGSFIELD_SOUND=off

# Live generation tests (tests/test_live_generation.py) — they SPEND MONEY, so they run only when
# this is exactly 1, with the variables above set and a real reference photo.
# OMEMO_LIVE_GENERATION=1
# OMEMO_LIVE_REFERENCE_PHOTO=/path/to/a/reference/photo.jpg

# --- Clip post text (ADR-0072) ---------------------------------------------------------
# The Notion review database's two rich_text properties where the model's draft is shown and the
# reviewer edits it before deciding. Set both or neither.
# OMEMO_REVIEW_NOTION_POST_TITLE_PROPERTY="Заголовок поста"
# OMEMO_REVIEW_NOTION_POST_DESCRIPTION_PROPERTY="Описание поста"
# The role clip_post_writer@v1 needs its own provider binding, like every role (ADR-0016/0029/0052):
# OMEMO_PROVIDER__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=anthropic
# OMEMO_MODEL__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=claude-sonnet-5
# OMEMO_INPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=...
# OMEMO_OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_MILLION__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=...
# OMEMO_PRICE_CURRENCY__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=USD
# OMEMO_MAX_TOKENS__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=16000
# OMEMO_THINKING__CLIP_POST_WRITER_V1=adaptive

# --- Auto-posting through upload-post (ADR-0073) ----------------------------------------
# With the key set, every approved clip is posted and the Run completes only after. The profile is
# the upload-post profile the platforms are connected to. Privacy is required: whether the channel
# sees a post is the maintainer's call, never a default.
# OMEMO_UPLOAD_POST_API_KEY="..."
# OMEMO_UPLOAD_POST_PROFILE="concept"
# OMEMO_UPLOAD_POST_PLATFORMS="youtube"          # comma list; default youtube
# OMEMO_UPLOAD_POST_YOUTUBE_PRIVACY="unlisted"   # public | unlisted | private
